<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Gallic Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">260 CE – 274 CE · capital Augusta Treverorum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Breakaway Roman state in Gaul, Britain and for a time Hispania, set up by Postumus in 260 when the empire seemed unable to defend its frontiers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 260, after the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valerian">Valerian</a> was captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> and Germanic invaders broke across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/postumus">Postumus</a> was proclaimed emperor by his troops. He besieged <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a> and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallienus">Gallienus</a>' son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saloninus">Saloninus</a> there and won the loyalty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germania">Germania</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Gallic emperors kept Roman institutions, with their own consuls, praetorian guard and mints at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>. They did not march on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> but concentrated on defending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/postumus">Postumus</a> was murdered by his troops in 269, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marius-emperor">Marius</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victorinus">Victorinus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetricus-i">Tetricus I</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> returned to the central empire early, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victorinus">Victorinus</a> was murdered in 271. In 274 Aurelian defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetricus-i">Tetricus</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalons-en-champagne">Châlons</a>, where Tetricus seems to have abandoned his army. He was paraded in Aurelian's triumph and then given an office in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and the provinces rejoined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gallic-empire.jpg" alt="Gallic Empire" width="320" height="336"><figcaption>Image: Original - ArdadN; edit - Wario2. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GallicEmpire262.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>260 CE – 274 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Augusta Treverorum</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Postumus, Victorinus, Tetricus I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a>, <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>, <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Imperium Galliarum</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=267&amp;focus=gallic-empire" aria-label="Gallic Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4838 411 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gallic Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5158 667L5020 640M5158 667L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5020 640h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5158 667h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5158 667h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=267&amp;focus=gallic-empire">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
